#: includes/settings-page.php:169
msgid "Content Protection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:172
msgid "Apply Protection to Post Types"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:182
msgid "Choose which post types to apply content protection to."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:187
msgid "Content Protection Mode"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:192
msgid "No Protection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:196
msgid "Encrypt Content (decode via JS)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:200
msgid "Encrypting the content helps prevent crawlers from reading raw HTML. Do not enable if you need SEO access."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:202
msgid "Decryption uses the browser's built-in Web Crypto API. The bundled CryptoJS fallback (about 60 KB) is only loaded on sites not served over HTTPS, or on demand in the rare browser without Web Crypto support."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:208
msgid "Custom Encryption Key"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:211
msgid "Use a unique key for this website. Leave blank to use default key from plugin constant."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:216
msgid "Decryption Key Delivery"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:221
msgid "Inline (default)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:225
msgid "Enhanced (fetch key via REST API after page load)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:229
msgid "Inline puts the key directly in page HTML (simple, works everywhere, but readable via view-source). Enhanced fetches the key from a REST API endpoint instead, keeping it out of cached/static HTML — better against basic scrapers and compatible with full-page caching. Neither mode makes content truly secret to a determined visitor running the page's own JavaScript. This endpoint is not rate-limited by the plugin; use your server/CDN/WAF if you need that."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:236
msgid "Enable Headless Browser Detection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:241
msgid "Withhold decryption from sessions that look like an automated browser (Puppeteer, Playwright, Selenium)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:244
msgid "Only takes effect when Content Protection Mode is set to Encrypt — it has no effect in \"No Protection\" mode, since there is no decryption step left to withhold. Scores several client-side automation signals together, so no single false-positive flag can block a real visitor on its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:246
msgid "This raises the cost of automated scraping but cannot detect every setup — well-configured \"stealth\" automation tooling can evade individual signals. Treat it as an extra deterrent layer, not a guarantee."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:252
msgid "Content Selector (for JS injection)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:255
msgid "Auto-detect"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: example CSS selector wrapped in <code>
#: includes/settings-page.php:260
#, php-format
msgid "CSS selector to locate content wrapper. Used for decryption and JS protection. Example: %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:265
msgid "\"Auto-detect\" loads your most recent published post in the background and tests common theme selectors against it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:272
msgid "Enable JavaScript Content Protection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:277
msgid "Block printing, prevent right-click and text selection, and interfere with browser developer tools."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:280
msgid "Blocks copying, selecting, printing, and inspecting content via JS. Includes right-click disable, keyboard shortcut blocking (Ctrl/⌘ + C, P, U, etc.), and DevTools interference."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:285
msgid "Advanced Browser Protection (Experimental)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:289
msgid "Enable Advanced DevTools Blocking"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:294
msgid "Actively detect when browser DevTools are opened (not just keyboard shortcuts) and close or redirect away from the tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:297
msgid "Uses the third-party \"disable-devtool\" library alongside the basic protection above. Independent of \"Enable JavaScript Content Protection\" — use either one alone, or both together."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:299
msgid "When DevTools stay open, this tries to close the tab; if the browser blocks that (the common case, since most browsers only allow closing tabs a script itself opened), it redirects the visitor back to your homepage instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:301
msgid "On the homepage itself the page content is hidden instead of redirected, so a false detection can never cause an endless reload loop."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:308
msgid "Enable Anti-Screenshot Protection (Init AntiSnap)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:313
msgid "Detect scroll-jump and DevTools-triggered layout patterns typical of automated screenshot or scraping tools, and briefly blur the page with a warning."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:316
msgid "Real readers scrolling and resizing normally are not affected. The blur clears itself automatically after a few seconds, or as soon as the tab regains focus."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:318
msgid "Init AntiSnap 6.0 only reacts to the evenly spaced, step-by-step jumps that scroll-and-stitch capture tools make — not to find-in-page, anchor links, scrollbar dragging, zooming, or pop-ups that lock page scrolling."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:325
msgid "Inject Noise"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:330
msgid "Insert invisible junk spans randomly to confuse crawlers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:332
msgid "Invisible to real readers. Junk spans use display: none."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:338
msgid "Noise Injection Rate"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:342
msgid "Chance (per word) of inserting a noise span. Higher values confuse crawlers more but add more hidden markup to the page. 1–50%, default 7%."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:347
msgid "Sensitive Keywords to Obscure"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: example comma-separated keyword list wrapped in <code>
#: includes/settings-page.php:354
#, php-format
msgid "Enter keywords to hide. Separate by commas. Example: %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:359
msgid "These will be replaced visually using CSS pseudo-elements and hidden from raw HTML."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:364
msgid "Global Exceptions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:367
msgid "Exclude User Roles"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:378
msgid "This applies to every protection feature on this page at once — Content Protection Mode, JavaScript Content Protection, Advanced DevTools Blocking, Anti-Screenshot Protection, Inject Noise, and Sensitive Keywords. Selected roles are fully excluded from all of them together and will always see the original, unprotected content — you can't exclude a role from just one feature."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:388
msgid "Important Notes When Using This Plugin:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:390
msgid "Use encryption only if you understand its impact on SEO, caching, and content accessibility."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:391
msgid "JavaScript protection relies on client-side execution. It can be bypassed by experienced users."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:392
msgid "For best results, combine multiple protection layers (encryption, JS, keyword cloaking)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:393
msgid "This plugin does not prevent content theft 100%. It raises the difficulty level for scraping."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:394
msgid "DevTools blocking, anti-screenshot detection, and headless browser detection are all heuristic and best-effort. They can occasionally trigger on unusual browsers/extensions, and can be bypassed by a determined user or well-configured automation tooling — treat them as an extra deterrent layer, not a guarantee."
msgstr ""

#: init-content-protector.php:348
msgid "⚠️ Automated screenshot or scraping tool detected. Action blocked!"
msgstr ""

